1
00:00:00,460 --> 00:00:02,820
Welcome back to Amnesia the Bunker.

2
00:00:03,520 --> 00:00:05,420
Now, I just got over a little bit of a sickness.

3
00:00:05,880 --> 00:00:09,220
Had some throat and nose issues, but that part is over now.

4
00:00:09,260 --> 00:00:09,880
Now I have a headache.

5
00:00:10,520 --> 00:00:15,080
I was gonna wait one more day to record this just to be sure I'm 100%, you know?

6
00:00:15,520 --> 00:00:20,200
But then my sister wrote me and was like, Dude, where's the next Amnesia episode?

7
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:21,040
I wanna watch it.

8
00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:23,220
So I felt a little bad and now I'm here recording it.

9
00:00:23,720 --> 00:00:24,940
So this one's for you, nerd.

10
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:26,760
Anyway...

11
00:00:28,180 --> 00:00:30,360
It's been a little while since I played last.

12
00:00:30,360 --> 00:00:32,360
We just arrived in the Roman tunnels.

13
00:00:33,620 --> 00:00:35,220
So I'm a little excited about that.

14
00:00:35,580 --> 00:00:36,960
Also, I did check the VOD.

15
00:00:38,940 --> 00:00:40,500
And this is the last note we got.

16
00:00:41,360 --> 00:00:42,940
Yeah, I'm gonna read that in a moment.

17
00:00:43,220 --> 00:00:48,180
And the reason I say in a moment... And by the way, feel free to skip through this part now.

18
00:00:48,380 --> 00:00:53,100
But I wanna take a little bit of time and review all the stuff we found so far.

19
00:00:53,840 --> 00:00:56,380
Just because there's information about these tunnels down here.

20
00:00:56,800 --> 00:00:57,680
Uh, in the notes.

21
00:00:58,120 --> 00:01:00,460
And maybe that can help me overcome my fear, you know?

22
00:01:00,640 --> 00:01:04,340
If I know what I'm getting myself into here, it should probably help.

23
00:01:04,780 --> 00:01:09,060
Also, I'm just in general interested in knowing what the hell is going on with the story here.

24
00:01:09,420 --> 00:01:12,040
Like, I think I have an idea, but I just wanna confirm things, you know?

25
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:13,380
Okay, let's see.

26
00:01:13,920 --> 00:01:14,820
Dr. Josinski.

27
00:01:15,720 --> 00:01:17,600
Rats and burnt corpses, that's not interesting.

28
00:01:18,640 --> 00:01:19,460
Amnesia Koss.

29
00:01:20,080 --> 00:01:21,600
Yeah, why did we get Amnesia?

30
00:01:22,060 --> 00:01:23,660
Was it just from the explosion or what?

31
00:01:26,040 --> 00:01:27,100
Initial head trauma?

32
00:01:27,300 --> 00:01:27,480
Yeah.

33
00:01:28,540 --> 00:01:28,860
Okay.

34
00:01:31,380 --> 00:01:31,380
Okay.

35
00:01:31,380 --> 00:01:32,480
Autopsy of Renard.

36
00:01:32,920 --> 00:01:35,560
Multiple lacerations, chest cavity torn to shreds.

37
00:01:35,620 --> 00:01:36,380
Yeah, this is the monster.

38
00:01:38,460 --> 00:01:39,860
Um, okay.

39
00:01:40,160 --> 00:01:41,340
This is my notes.

40
00:01:41,540 --> 00:01:42,040
So...

41
00:01:42,860 --> 00:01:48,280
I did some sleight of hand, and I fooled Lambert, and made him go on patrol, right?

42
00:01:49,240 --> 00:01:51,120
Uh, just to recap this, I remember this.

43
00:01:51,920 --> 00:01:54,740
Uh, and I felt so bad about it, because he didn't return from patrol.

44
00:01:55,800 --> 00:01:58,880
So, you know, I was agonizing over it, and...

45
00:01:59,380 --> 00:02:01,760
Then I snuck out, and tried to find him.

46
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:04,520
And that's where the game starts, right?

47
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:06,520
Uh, cause we find him in a hole.

48
00:02:07,820 --> 00:02:12,180
But then all kinds of shit happens, and we do get out, but he had to carry us out.

49
00:02:12,780 --> 00:02:13,140
Right?

50
00:02:13,220 --> 00:02:14,380
There was an explosion and all that.

51
00:02:15,120 --> 00:02:15,360
Yeah.

52
00:02:15,700 --> 00:02:16,900
And this was the 9th of July.

53
00:02:18,460 --> 00:02:21,660
My conscience compels me now, as it failed to compel me then.

54
00:02:22,820 --> 00:02:23,840
I love that sentence.

55
00:02:26,060 --> 00:02:26,780
Uh, Freelo...

56
00:02:27,580 --> 00:02:28,400
And what is this?

57
00:02:28,500 --> 00:02:29,060
Dog tags?

58
00:02:29,160 --> 00:02:29,660
Okay, fine.

59
00:02:30,240 --> 00:02:31,120
Fuel and fire.

60
00:02:31,620 --> 00:02:32,340
Yeah, yeah, whatever.

61
00:02:33,080 --> 00:02:33,880
How to get out of here?

62
00:02:33,980 --> 00:02:36,640
Yeah, we gotta get the detonator from the Roman tunnels.

63
00:02:36,740 --> 00:02:37,400
That's why we're here.

64
00:02:38,520 --> 00:02:40,720
I go now to try to retrieve them both.

65
00:02:41,080 --> 00:02:41,940
This guy failed.

66
00:02:42,560 --> 00:02:43,080
Obviously.

67
00:02:44,300 --> 00:02:44,820
Wrench.

68
00:02:45,260 --> 00:02:46,220
Unknown author.

69
00:02:47,520 --> 00:02:49,360
Yeah, keep the lights on, that's fine.

70
00:02:50,480 --> 00:02:50,800
Joubert.

71
00:02:51,580 --> 00:02:52,700
Roman tunnel update.

72
00:02:52,940 --> 00:02:54,340
I think I'm gonna read some of this again.

73
00:02:55,660 --> 00:02:59,900
Uh, engineers have broken through our storage area, and into the old Roman tunnels.

74
00:03:00,340 --> 00:03:01,540
They are as we thought.

75
00:03:02,080 --> 00:03:05,860
Structurally sound, deep, and I confess I was skeptical of this last point.

76
00:03:05,860 --> 00:03:08,980
But they do indeed lead in the direction of the German line.

77
00:03:09,540 --> 00:03:10,920
Right, that's why they did this.

78
00:03:11,120 --> 00:03:15,180
To get, uh, into an ambush attack or something, right?

79
00:03:16,100 --> 00:03:19,880
By September we should be in position to launch a massive push from inside the tunnels.

80
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:20,420
Yeah, exactly.

81
00:03:21,700 --> 00:03:25,840
Perhaps of note, inside the tunnels we found urns, Latin texts, etc.

82
00:03:26,320 --> 00:03:29,060
We'll do our best to preserve some materials for posterity.

83
00:03:29,920 --> 00:03:30,400
Okay.

84
00:03:31,540 --> 00:03:35,460
And this was on the 2nd of May, so quite a bit before.

85
00:03:35,860 --> 00:03:37,880
I went out to try and retrieve Lambert.

86
00:03:39,100 --> 00:03:40,320
This is the 10th of July.

87
00:03:40,480 --> 00:03:41,860
This is the day after we came home.

88
00:03:42,940 --> 00:03:44,700
And I guess we had amnesia at this point.

89
00:03:45,740 --> 00:03:47,300
Uh, odd occurrences last night.

90
00:03:48,020 --> 00:03:50,920
Uh, Soldat Lambert, this is what someone in the comments told me.

91
00:03:50,980 --> 00:03:52,540
This is Soldat, apparently.

92
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:57,920
Uh, Lambert thought dead after his patrol on the 8th, returned to the barracks in fine health.

93
00:03:58,300 --> 00:04:02,540
He carried with him Soldat Clément, that's me, severely wounded from an explosion.

94
00:04:03,220 --> 00:04:04,680
Lambert reports the following.

95
00:04:04,920 --> 00:04:09,060
That midway through his patrol on the 8th, he fell into a deep crater and was unable to escape.

96
00:04:09,720 --> 00:04:15,820
Clément, his close friend, snuck out after him last night, located him in the crater, and carried him out.

97
00:04:16,380 --> 00:04:18,420
They were spotted in the ensuing attack.

98
00:04:18,760 --> 00:04:20,400
Clément was injured by an explosion.

99
00:04:20,640 --> 00:04:22,640
It fell on Lambert to carry him back.

100
00:04:23,160 --> 00:04:23,840
Yeah, what a bro.

101
00:04:25,640 --> 00:04:32,340
Very odd that Lambert was neither injured from the fall nor the explosion, and that he ended up saving the man who came to save him.

102
00:04:32,800 --> 00:04:33,840
Yeah, that is weird.

103
00:04:34,080 --> 00:04:36,020
But battlefield luck is an odd thing.

104
00:04:36,320 --> 00:04:39,040
In every life, fate's winds blow erratic.

105
00:04:39,840 --> 00:04:40,880
That's a nice sentence.

106
00:04:41,920 --> 00:04:48,420
Judging by Lambert's description, the crater he fell into seems to have been located very close to the Roman tunnels we unearthed.

107
00:04:48,700 --> 00:04:50,860
It may have been a result of work down there.

108
00:04:51,720 --> 00:04:57,560
Recommend a future patrol investigate and make sure we have not opened up a back door into our own bunker.

109
00:04:58,200 --> 00:04:59,360
Yeah, that's a good point.

110
00:05:00,340 --> 00:05:03,060
Don't want the Germans just pouring in like that.

111
00:05:04,220 --> 00:05:05,960
Okay, so the 14th of July.

112
00:05:06,460 --> 00:05:07,840
That's like four days later.

113
00:05:08,300 --> 00:05:08,520
Night.

114
00:05:09,420 --> 00:05:14,300
Strange scratching sounds a few moments ago, and now it sounds like someone is pacing in the hallway.

115
00:05:14,880 --> 00:05:15,760
Probably Renard.

116
00:05:16,100 --> 00:05:18,320
Drunk on the stash of wine I know he hides from us.

117
00:05:19,220 --> 00:05:20,540
Best I confront him now.

118
00:05:20,860 --> 00:05:24,720
Either get him into bed to sleep it off or convince him to share a bottle or two with me.

119
00:05:25,700 --> 00:05:26,180
Smart.

120
00:05:26,600 --> 00:05:27,600
The day after.

121
00:05:28,240 --> 00:05:30,460
Cold fear runs through all our veins now.

122
00:05:31,280 --> 00:05:33,160
Fournier has terrorized the men for answers.

123
00:05:33,460 --> 00:05:36,040
They say they were asleep until Renard screams.

124
00:05:36,420 --> 00:05:37,640
I believe them, of course.

125
00:05:38,480 --> 00:05:43,160
Fournier went so far as to accuse the prisoner of escaping his cell and committing the murder.

126
00:05:43,680 --> 00:05:44,160
Impossible.

127
00:05:44,980 --> 00:05:46,360
Yeah, I don't believe so either.

128
00:05:46,820 --> 00:05:49,120
It is the monster, which I believe is Lambert.

129
00:05:49,520 --> 00:05:51,220
I mean, it just makes sense, right?

130
00:05:51,500 --> 00:05:53,000
We come back from patrol.

131
00:05:53,580 --> 00:05:55,820
The day after, or was it four days after?

132
00:05:56,280 --> 00:05:57,660
Shit started going down.

133
00:05:58,000 --> 00:05:58,400
Right?

134
00:05:58,820 --> 00:06:00,180
I worry about Fournier.

135
00:06:00,480 --> 00:06:01,660
His rage hides fear.

136
00:06:01,920 --> 00:06:04,740
He takes it out on the men and I can see no way to stop it.

137
00:06:05,020 --> 00:06:06,360
It breeds contempt.

138
00:06:07,980 --> 00:06:10,660
My mind slips back to the moment Renard started screaming.

139
00:06:10,940 --> 00:06:12,540
How easily it could have been me.

140
00:06:12,840 --> 00:06:14,440
How easily it still could be.

141
00:06:15,660 --> 00:06:18,040
For the first time, I wish the order to attack would come.

142
00:06:18,520 --> 00:06:21,860
I would rather face a thousand German guns than this nameless dread.

143
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:24,260
Yep, I agree.

144
00:06:24,820 --> 00:06:26,160
I could not do that either.

145
00:06:26,860 --> 00:06:31,560
Like, if I was here in real life in this bunker, I would have pointed this gun straight to my own head.

146
00:06:31,560 --> 00:06:32,940
A long time ago.

147
00:06:33,140 --> 00:06:33,880
And pulled the trigger.

148
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:35,880
It's too scary.

149
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:36,660
I just can't do it.

150
00:06:36,980 --> 00:06:37,440
But who knows?

151
00:06:37,560 --> 00:06:38,800
Maybe the body kicks in.

152
00:06:39,040 --> 00:06:41,500
You know, survival instincts, adrenaline, I don't know.

153
00:06:41,840 --> 00:06:44,180
I guess you'll never know until you're in this situation.

154
00:06:45,720 --> 00:06:47,100
Uh, Joubert's final journal.

155
00:06:47,380 --> 00:06:48,720
To any who find this.

156
00:06:49,060 --> 00:06:50,300
Also, no date on it.

157
00:06:50,960 --> 00:06:53,620
Fournier, our commanding officer, cowers next to me now.

158
00:06:53,880 --> 00:06:55,840
He's lost his mind to an abyss of fear.

159
00:06:56,060 --> 00:06:58,340
He repeats the same refrain over and over.

160
00:06:58,860 --> 00:07:01,220
We must flee and seal the beast where it belongs.

161
00:07:01,840 --> 00:07:02,860
He wants to run.

162
00:07:03,040 --> 00:07:04,360
To blow up the exit behind him.

163
00:07:04,780 --> 00:07:07,280
Sealing the demon down here, the demon and our men.

164
00:07:07,760 --> 00:07:09,000
His constant refrain.

165
00:07:09,300 --> 00:07:10,300
It is getting to me.

166
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:12,300
And that same void of terror.

167
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:14,160
It is also overtaking me.

168
00:07:14,800 --> 00:07:16,240
To any of my men who see this.

169
00:07:16,660 --> 00:07:19,640
Once we're free of this place, I will get the arsenal code from him.

170
00:07:19,940 --> 00:07:22,100
I will get it and I will radio it back to you.

171
00:07:23,100 --> 00:07:24,320
Wow, thanks dude.

172
00:07:25,040 --> 00:07:26,380
Trapped down here with that beast?

173
00:07:26,380 --> 00:07:28,360
The arsenal may be your only hope.

174
00:07:28,720 --> 00:07:29,660
It's all I can do.

175
00:07:29,840 --> 00:07:31,020
All I have courage to do.

176
00:07:31,840 --> 00:07:34,080
Get to the communications room in the soldier quarters.

177
00:07:34,360 --> 00:07:35,000
Hide there.

178
00:07:35,440 --> 00:07:36,900
I'll broadcast the code to you.

179
00:07:37,280 --> 00:07:37,620
Joubert.

180
00:07:38,580 --> 00:07:40,200
What a fucking rat.

181
00:07:41,540 --> 00:07:44,040
So he actually escaped with all the other officers.

182
00:07:44,160 --> 00:07:45,760
I mean, we knew this already, but it's just...

183
00:07:46,380 --> 00:07:48,960
When we've been through all of this, it just makes it worse, you know?

184
00:07:49,720 --> 00:07:53,020
Like, he escapes with all the other officers, blows the shit up behind him.

185
00:07:53,620 --> 00:07:56,100
And then he's like, oh, it's okay, because I'm gonna give you the code.

186
00:07:56,220 --> 00:07:56,560
Good luck!

187
00:07:56,840 --> 00:07:57,280
You know?

188
00:07:57,900 --> 00:07:59,140
As if that's gonna help me.

189
00:07:59,220 --> 00:08:00,460
I guess it did help me, but still.

190
00:08:02,340 --> 00:08:02,940
Little rat.

191
00:08:05,420 --> 00:08:06,020
LaRue's report.

192
00:08:07,620 --> 00:08:08,160
15th of May.

193
00:08:08,260 --> 00:08:10,240
So this was way before all of this.

194
00:08:11,500 --> 00:08:14,540
From Soldat LaRue to Fournier and Blanchett.

195
00:08:15,020 --> 00:08:18,640
I am now putting into writing what I have reported to both of my immediate superiors.

196
00:08:19,720 --> 00:08:24,640
Last evening, 14th of May, I was assigned to aid the engineers in mapping the Roman tunnels.

197
00:08:25,680 --> 00:08:32,480
As I entered the deepest area of the tunnels, I noticed a strange glowing liquid seeping from the walls right.

198
00:08:33,900 --> 00:08:40,840
When I turned around, the walls of the tunnels themselves were suddenly gone, and I was standing in a vast plain of darkness.

199
00:08:41,860 --> 00:08:45,420
In the distance, there was a sickly light that seemed to be calling me forward.

200
00:08:45,920 --> 00:08:48,980
Between it and me, malformed shadows moved.

201
00:08:50,560 --> 00:08:54,680
There's definitely some kind of, uh, hallucinogenic thing going on here.

202
00:08:55,020 --> 00:08:55,640
You know?

203
00:08:56,820 --> 00:08:57,880
I blinked again.

204
00:08:58,140 --> 00:08:58,880
It was gone.

205
00:08:59,220 --> 00:09:00,520
I was back in the tunnel.

206
00:09:00,940 --> 00:09:02,520
It lasted but a split second.

207
00:09:02,800 --> 00:09:05,560
But I'm quite convinced that what I saw was no daydream.

208
00:09:05,780 --> 00:09:06,740
It was real.

209
00:09:07,440 --> 00:09:09,460
Since that experience, I have felt haunted.

210
00:09:09,720 --> 00:09:11,260
Like a part of me is still there.

211
00:09:11,540 --> 00:09:12,500
Stuck in the tunnels.

212
00:09:12,960 --> 00:09:15,600
I keep seeing shapes moving at the edges of my vision.

213
00:09:16,060 --> 00:09:18,220
I am formally requesting medical leave.

214
00:09:18,220 --> 00:09:19,580
Please help me.

215
00:09:20,780 --> 00:09:21,540
Oh, man.

216
00:09:22,720 --> 00:09:23,200
Stafford.

217
00:09:23,840 --> 00:09:24,840
Daisy chain switches.

218
00:09:24,840 --> 00:09:25,660
Not interesting.

219
00:09:26,540 --> 00:09:27,500
No to a dead friend.

220
00:09:28,480 --> 00:09:28,860
Uh, yeah.

221
00:09:28,960 --> 00:09:29,840
Go to pillbox.

222
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:30,660
Pillbox key.

223
00:09:31,820 --> 00:09:33,360
And Toussaint Befaux.

224
00:09:34,760 --> 00:09:35,700
This is his journal.

225
00:09:35,820 --> 00:09:36,600
The 16th of May.

226
00:09:37,100 --> 00:09:38,640
Still, way before any of this happened.

227
00:09:39,660 --> 00:09:41,800
Neuer has been telling us of the tunnel texts.

228
00:09:42,340 --> 00:09:44,160
Describing what these tunnels were used for.

229
00:09:45,260 --> 00:09:46,740
But I didn't need him to tell me.

230
00:09:46,920 --> 00:09:47,820
I've seen it.

231
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:49,340
I was in there, in the dark.

232
00:09:49,780 --> 00:09:51,500
I dream of it every night now.

233
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:55,420
Dreams are so real that when I wake, the day itself feels like the dream.

234
00:09:56,380 --> 00:09:57,320
I'm at a ritual.

235
00:09:57,660 --> 00:09:59,600
It begins with the drinking of a liquid.

236
00:09:59,840 --> 00:10:00,780
Sweet and thick.

237
00:10:01,160 --> 00:10:02,480
Like mucus or honey.

238
00:10:03,080 --> 00:10:04,160
Repulsive and yet intoxicating.

239
00:10:05,200 --> 00:10:08,120
It's gotta be that liquid that was seeping from the tunnels, right?

240
00:10:09,380 --> 00:10:10,700
As I drink, it warms my body.

241
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:13,360
Fills me with a lust for all things carnal.

242
00:10:13,740 --> 00:10:14,180
Sex.

243
00:10:14,420 --> 00:10:14,700
Blood.

244
00:10:15,120 --> 00:10:15,400
Flesh.

245
00:10:16,400 --> 00:10:17,660
Around me are others.

246
00:10:17,960 --> 00:10:19,040
Their faces hidden.

247
00:10:19,360 --> 00:10:20,340
Their bodies rippling.

248
00:10:20,640 --> 00:10:23,340
I know we all serve the same master to the same end.

249
00:10:23,700 --> 00:10:25,720
A place in her unending kingdom.

250
00:10:27,700 --> 00:10:28,260
Her?

251
00:10:28,900 --> 00:10:29,800
Unending kingdom?

252
00:10:30,900 --> 00:10:31,180
Interesting.

253
00:10:32,400 --> 00:10:32,880
Immortality.

254
00:10:33,220 --> 00:10:34,800
The things I do in these dreams.

255
00:10:35,200 --> 00:10:36,920
A terrible whirl of horrors.

256
00:10:37,180 --> 00:10:38,240
Bloody and twirled.

257
00:10:38,400 --> 00:10:41,220
That make the charnel pit of the war seem like mere play.

258
00:10:41,860 --> 00:10:44,500
I wake horrified, but in the dreams I am elated.

259
00:10:44,940 --> 00:10:45,940
The worst part?

260
00:10:46,180 --> 00:10:48,220
At the end of every day, I wanna be asleep.

261
00:10:48,580 --> 00:10:50,160
I wanna go back to that place.

262
00:10:50,400 --> 00:10:51,700
I wanna feel that way.

263
00:10:52,020 --> 00:10:55,240
I want the violence and the ecstasy and the pitch black darkness.

264
00:10:55,820 --> 00:10:57,420
It's fucking crazy, dude.

265
00:10:59,320 --> 00:11:01,060
I'm gonna wait with this until the end.

266
00:11:01,240 --> 00:11:02,120
We're gonna read this at the end.

267
00:11:02,800 --> 00:11:04,060
Uh, Alex Neuer.

268
00:11:04,860 --> 00:11:05,640
Part 1.

269
00:11:06,560 --> 00:11:07,460
30th of April.

270
00:11:07,620 --> 00:11:09,220
Okay, so this is even earlier.

271
00:11:10,180 --> 00:11:12,160
Finally got some answers from the engineering team.

272
00:11:12,660 --> 00:11:15,460
Command believes there are old Roman tunnels adjacent to our position.

273
00:11:15,640 --> 00:11:17,120
They're opening them this evening.

274
00:11:17,820 --> 00:11:19,960
Command hopes to use them to launch a surprise attack.

275
00:11:20,180 --> 00:11:22,820
As if any attack at this point could be termed surprise.

276
00:11:23,280 --> 00:11:24,160
This is a war.

277
00:11:24,540 --> 00:11:26,700
We are all always expecting an attack.

278
00:11:27,460 --> 00:11:28,720
Curious to see these tunnels, though.

279
00:11:29,080 --> 00:11:31,480
A little dash of antiquity would liven the place up.

280
00:11:31,820 --> 00:11:34,780
It had certainly helped keep my mind off the daily grind of the war.

281
00:11:35,400 --> 00:11:36,440
I guess so, yeah.

282
00:11:37,440 --> 00:11:40,320
9th of May, so quite a bit in the future there.

283
00:11:40,820 --> 00:11:42,280
Or at least 10 days or so.

284
00:11:42,680 --> 00:11:45,980
The officers presented me today with a rather unexpected and strange gift.

285
00:11:46,660 --> 00:11:48,880
Aging texts from inside the Roman tunnels.

286
00:11:49,420 --> 00:11:51,260
Seems they got word of my interests.

287
00:11:51,260 --> 00:11:55,080
I took them, of course, but the truth is these texts are far too fragile.

288
00:11:55,460 --> 00:11:57,640
Too valuable to survive life in this horrid place.

289
00:11:58,360 --> 00:11:59,880
They require more delicate hands.

290
00:12:00,160 --> 00:12:01,440
More learned minds than mine.

291
00:12:02,960 --> 00:12:04,480
Still, curiosity reigns.

292
00:12:05,200 --> 00:12:08,380
So Neuer was the guy who was really interested in the...

293
00:12:08,380 --> 00:12:10,500
academic side of things here.

294
00:12:12,160 --> 00:12:12,960
11th of May.

295
00:12:13,400 --> 00:12:15,300
This morning Ackerman died of his wounds.

296
00:12:15,720 --> 00:12:18,840
I'd only known him a time, but considered him one of my better friends here.

297
00:12:18,840 --> 00:12:20,580
I hope heaven welcomes him.

298
00:12:21,080 --> 00:12:24,920
To distract myself, I have been going over the texts and have had quite the shock.

299
00:12:25,180 --> 00:12:27,840
These texts are not Roman in origin.

300
00:12:28,380 --> 00:12:31,340
The language is Latin, or Latinate at least.

301
00:12:31,720 --> 00:12:35,360
But what they're writing about has no relation to what I know of Roman culture.

302
00:12:35,600 --> 00:12:36,620
From any era.

303
00:12:37,020 --> 00:12:40,760
The texts seem to be of a religious or at least superstitious nature.

304
00:12:40,760 --> 00:12:42,540
A phrase is repeated.

305
00:12:42,980 --> 00:12:44,800
To cross into the darkness beyond.

306
00:12:45,200 --> 00:12:46,960
And then something about sight.

307
00:12:48,940 --> 00:12:50,180
Like seeing things?

308
00:12:50,320 --> 00:12:51,000
Seeing visions?

309
00:12:51,400 --> 00:12:51,960
Maybe?

310
00:12:52,760 --> 00:12:53,360
Hallucinations?

311
00:12:55,240 --> 00:12:56,160
13th of May.

312
00:12:56,720 --> 00:12:57,560
Haven't slept.

313
00:12:57,700 --> 00:12:58,460
Need to get this down.

314
00:12:58,680 --> 00:13:00,740
The texts are of a religious nature.

315
00:13:01,260 --> 00:13:06,120
Whoever these ancient people were, they believed that they had found a means to immortality.

316
00:13:06,120 --> 00:13:10,700
And to achieve this goal, they needed access to what they thought was some other world.

317
00:13:10,980 --> 00:13:13,480
One dominated by darkness and ruled by...

318
00:13:13,480 --> 00:13:14,240
I don't know.

319
00:13:14,520 --> 00:13:16,320
They use words I can't translate.

320
00:13:16,860 --> 00:13:18,160
Ruled by some thing.

321
00:13:19,040 --> 00:13:19,300
Ooh.

322
00:13:20,260 --> 00:13:23,420
They claimed that dark other world was full of spirits.

323
00:13:23,820 --> 00:13:24,320
Monsters.

324
00:13:24,520 --> 00:13:27,460
And that the air there was endlessly alive with cries of torment.

325
00:13:27,700 --> 00:13:29,960
And the sickly rattle of souls near death.

326
00:13:30,820 --> 00:13:32,740
That is what they were using the tunnels for.

327
00:13:32,740 --> 00:13:35,900
For them it was a doorway into some pagan hell.

328
00:13:36,460 --> 00:13:39,240
The texts are full of wild stories of blood orgies.

329
00:13:39,420 --> 00:13:40,740
Of sadistic spirits.

330
00:13:41,040 --> 00:13:45,520
Of the awful things these men and women would do to each other in worship of darkness.

331
00:13:46,300 --> 00:13:51,300
They speak at length of some substance that is meant to grant the worthy some kind of immortality in darkness.

332
00:13:52,220 --> 00:13:53,500
I'm on patrol tonight.

333
00:13:53,840 --> 00:13:55,040
Need to sleep before then.

334
00:13:55,460 --> 00:13:56,520
But then I'm back at this.

335
00:13:57,520 --> 00:13:58,500
Oh, man.

336
00:13:58,640 --> 00:13:59,460
What is this liquid?

337
00:13:59,780 --> 00:14:00,740
This substance?

338
00:14:03,180 --> 00:14:06,120
Am I gonna find some of that substance down here now?

339
00:14:07,260 --> 00:14:11,580
Am I gonna be seeing visions and start hallucinating or something?

340
00:14:12,320 --> 00:14:14,560
Am I gonna go into pagan hell?

341
00:14:15,420 --> 00:14:16,200
I'm scared.

342
00:14:17,480 --> 00:14:18,820
Okay, 14th of May.

343
00:14:18,820 --> 00:14:22,660
I have spoken to no one of what's written in these texts.

344
00:14:22,940 --> 00:14:23,940
I swear it.

345
00:14:24,380 --> 00:14:28,040
But now LaRue comes out of the tunnels claiming to have seen things described in them.

346
00:14:28,700 --> 00:14:31,440
My rational mind cannot accept that this might be coincidence.

347
00:14:31,860 --> 00:14:33,520
Nor can it accept the alternative.

348
00:14:34,160 --> 00:14:36,360
I have to tell the others what's written in these texts.

349
00:14:36,680 --> 00:14:37,220
Tell them.

350
00:14:37,640 --> 00:14:38,260
Warn them.

351
00:14:39,440 --> 00:14:40,700
That is kind of crazy though.

352
00:14:41,060 --> 00:14:42,840
So there is something to it, you know?

353
00:14:43,540 --> 00:14:44,780
So who came out of the tunnels?

354
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:45,480
Did you say?

355
00:14:46,880 --> 00:14:47,280
LaRue.

356
00:14:47,520 --> 00:14:47,640
Okay.

357
00:14:49,040 --> 00:14:49,780
18th of May.

358
00:14:50,220 --> 00:14:52,820
They've punished LaRue for speaking out about what he saw.

359
00:14:53,120 --> 00:14:54,800
And now Renard has sent for me.

360
00:14:55,100 --> 00:14:56,800
I'm sure I'm to be punished as well.

361
00:14:57,460 --> 00:14:59,400
We're stuck between the Germans in front of us.

362
00:14:59,640 --> 00:15:00,900
High command behind us.

363
00:15:01,220 --> 00:15:04,860
And some other horrible force that seems to lurk in shadows all around us.

364
00:15:05,780 --> 00:15:08,020
Yeah, he's not talking about the monster at this point.

365
00:15:08,320 --> 00:15:09,680
Because this didn't happen yet.

366
00:15:10,780 --> 00:15:12,300
Uh, this is the 18th of May.

367
00:15:12,540 --> 00:15:15,080
He's talking about, uh, people seeing things.

368
00:15:15,980 --> 00:15:19,280
And these weird texts giving him the heebie-jeebies, you know?

369
00:15:19,760 --> 00:15:21,700
He's scared out of his mind because of it.

370
00:15:22,540 --> 00:15:24,940
I fear we are now truly beyond God's reach.

371
00:15:26,060 --> 00:15:27,580
Definitely stuck in a hard place here.

372
00:15:27,860 --> 00:15:28,900
The 20th of May.

373
00:15:29,480 --> 00:15:32,240
I've been locked in Delpy's cells for the past two nights.

374
00:15:32,940 --> 00:15:35,060
Renard's punishment for me speaking about the texts.

375
00:15:35,840 --> 00:15:37,260
Nightmare after nightmare there.

376
00:15:37,640 --> 00:15:38,720
Dreams of darkness.

377
00:15:39,480 --> 00:15:40,380
Seductive darkness.

378
00:15:41,180 --> 00:15:42,000
Voices there.

379
00:15:42,320 --> 00:15:43,080
Welcoming me.

380
00:15:43,700 --> 00:15:45,960
I returned to my bunk and was met with the men.

381
00:15:46,180 --> 00:15:48,040
All of whom now have tales to tell.

382
00:15:48,640 --> 00:15:49,160
Nicolet.

383
00:15:49,340 --> 00:15:49,800
Barber.

384
00:15:50,320 --> 00:15:50,840
Houlebeck.

385
00:15:51,100 --> 00:15:51,860
On and on.

386
00:15:52,160 --> 00:15:53,480
They're all hearing things.

387
00:15:53,880 --> 00:15:54,660
Dreaming things.

388
00:15:55,340 --> 00:15:55,580
Hmm.

389
00:15:57,520 --> 00:16:00,860
Nights are now spent in the grip of a fear that crawls up the spine.

390
00:16:00,860 --> 00:16:02,900
And digs its claws behind the eyes.

391
00:16:03,420 --> 00:16:04,480
Piercing mind and soul.

392
00:16:05,440 --> 00:16:07,300
But after what happened to LaRue and me.

393
00:16:07,760 --> 00:16:08,980
None dare speak to the officers.

394
00:16:09,420 --> 00:16:10,700
Not even to Joubert.

395
00:16:11,380 --> 00:16:11,900
And worse.

396
00:16:12,500 --> 00:16:13,420
Raids are beginning again.

397
00:16:13,920 --> 00:16:15,120
I'm to go tomorrow night.

398
00:16:16,500 --> 00:16:17,620
The 23rd.

399
00:16:18,260 --> 00:16:19,060
Back from the raid.

400
00:16:19,260 --> 00:16:19,820
Can't sleep.

401
00:16:20,260 --> 00:16:20,900
Shells falling.

402
00:16:21,380 --> 00:16:23,120
The soles of my boots are worn thin.

403
00:16:23,480 --> 00:16:25,240
My feet bloody and blistered.

404
00:16:25,760 --> 00:16:26,840
Lost too many out there.

405
00:16:27,240 --> 00:16:28,140
I feel trapped.

406
00:16:30,020 --> 00:16:30,840
25th of May.

407
00:16:31,540 --> 00:16:34,620
Last night the entire barracks was awakened by the sounds from the tunnel.

408
00:16:35,240 --> 00:16:36,400
Nightly they grow louder.

409
00:16:36,700 --> 00:16:38,740
When I slept I dreamt of other worlds.

410
00:16:39,060 --> 00:16:40,660
Of pain wrapped in ecstasy.

411
00:16:41,060 --> 00:16:43,080
This morning we are all as ghosts.

412
00:16:43,680 --> 00:16:45,140
Things cannot continue this way.

413
00:16:45,640 --> 00:16:48,580
I will enter the tunnels and see if I can find some way to end this.

414
00:16:48,780 --> 00:16:49,960
For all our sakes.

415
00:16:51,360 --> 00:16:51,880
Oh.

416
00:16:54,600 --> 00:16:55,120
Okay.

417
00:16:55,720 --> 00:16:59,320
Is that what started the whole mutiny thing then?

418
00:17:02,140 --> 00:17:03,180
Soldat Chouinard.

419
00:17:03,520 --> 00:17:04,420
The rats.

420
00:17:05,680 --> 00:17:08,060
Have you noticed how the rats have changed down here lately?

421
00:17:08,220 --> 00:17:08,920
Yeah, I have.

422
00:17:09,460 --> 00:17:11,320
Definitely because of the whole thing that's happening.

423
00:17:12,180 --> 00:17:13,600
Yeah, ever since they opened up those tunnels.

424
00:17:14,360 --> 00:17:17,020
The rats have been transformed as well.

425
00:17:17,020 --> 00:17:20,160
So there's definitely something going on with Lambert, right?

426
00:17:20,660 --> 00:17:22,260
The fact that he was in this hole.

427
00:17:22,480 --> 00:17:23,760
Right next to the tunnels.

428
00:17:25,960 --> 00:17:29,120
Maybe he was infected the same way that everyone else was.

429
00:17:29,520 --> 00:17:31,620
But for some reason for him it got worse.

430
00:17:31,620 --> 00:17:34,180
And he got turned into this monster.

431
00:17:35,360 --> 00:17:36,740
Fear and paranoia.

432
00:17:38,820 --> 00:17:40,900
Fournier claims one of us killed Renard.

433
00:17:41,220 --> 00:17:42,880
But I saw Renard's corpse.

434
00:17:43,220 --> 00:17:44,320
His eyes were gone.

435
00:17:44,840 --> 00:17:46,100
Gouged from his skull.

436
00:17:46,400 --> 00:17:47,640
His tongue was shredded.

437
00:17:48,200 --> 00:17:50,760
We all hated Renard, but none of us could have done this.

438
00:17:51,440 --> 00:17:52,720
War is a brutality.

439
00:17:53,060 --> 00:17:54,160
But it is anonymous.

440
00:17:54,720 --> 00:17:55,320
Mechanized.

441
00:17:55,600 --> 00:17:57,200
We fire at distant soldiers.

442
00:17:57,640 --> 00:17:58,740
Whoever did this.

443
00:17:59,200 --> 00:18:00,120
It was intimate.

444
00:18:00,440 --> 00:18:01,160
It was sadistic.

445
00:18:01,740 --> 00:18:03,140
I fear for all of us.

446
00:18:03,740 --> 00:18:03,960
Yeah.

447
00:18:04,240 --> 00:18:05,880
It was Lambert, I'm pretty sure.

448
00:18:06,200 --> 00:18:07,160
It can hear me.

449
00:18:07,280 --> 00:18:08,320
Also, this is July, right?

450
00:18:08,660 --> 00:18:09,100
So...

451
00:18:09,100 --> 00:18:10,840
This is after...

452
00:18:10,840 --> 00:18:10,960
What?

453
00:18:11,080 --> 00:18:12,800
Five days after we returned home.

454
00:18:13,800 --> 00:18:14,640
With Lambert.

455
00:18:16,640 --> 00:18:18,400
Dude, what if we are Lambert?

456
00:18:20,100 --> 00:18:21,900
And Clemong is actually the monster.

457
00:18:21,980 --> 00:18:22,900
We have Amnesia, right?

458
00:18:24,680 --> 00:18:26,040
What if we are Lambert?

459
00:18:28,640 --> 00:18:30,120
That would be such a cool twist.

460
00:18:31,720 --> 00:18:33,280
Oh my god, I hope that's the case.

461
00:18:33,400 --> 00:18:34,080
That would be awesome.

462
00:18:35,880 --> 00:18:36,860
It can hear me.

463
00:18:37,460 --> 00:18:39,640
Every time I take a step, I swear it can hear me.

464
00:18:40,120 --> 00:18:41,540
I've crawled into this hole here.

465
00:18:41,620 --> 00:18:42,180
I'll just wait.

466
00:18:42,820 --> 00:18:44,020
I'll just hold my breath and wait.

467
00:18:44,140 --> 00:18:45,160
Yeah, don't do that, dude.

468
00:18:45,280 --> 00:18:46,140
That's how this guy died.

469
00:18:48,300 --> 00:18:49,020
Johannes Nicolet.

470
00:18:49,780 --> 00:18:50,840
His unsent letter.

471
00:18:52,120 --> 00:18:53,260
To Amanda Nicolet.

472
00:18:53,260 --> 00:18:53,760
Okay.

473
00:18:53,760 --> 00:18:54,640
This was the 5th of May.

474
00:18:54,780 --> 00:18:54,920
Okay.

475
00:18:55,920 --> 00:18:57,320
So quite a bit before everything.

476
00:18:57,980 --> 00:18:59,480
Dearest, thank you for the package.

477
00:18:59,680 --> 00:19:01,460
I'm saving the chocolate for a special occasion.

478
00:19:01,720 --> 00:19:03,560
And I'm keeping the photo close to my heart.

479
00:19:03,900 --> 00:19:04,700
Wait, which photo?

480
00:19:06,780 --> 00:19:07,640
Is it this one?

481
00:19:08,220 --> 00:19:09,460
It's gotta be that one, right?

482
00:19:12,300 --> 00:19:12,700
Yeah.

483
00:19:12,700 --> 00:19:12,740
Yeah.

484
00:19:13,260 --> 00:19:16,120
It's been weeks now since I've been called for any combat action.

485
00:19:16,340 --> 00:19:18,840
But a new kind of fear is spreading inside the bunker.

486
00:19:19,460 --> 00:19:21,520
Last night, I woke with a chill.

487
00:19:21,820 --> 00:19:24,700
A strange sound was emanating from deeper in the bunker.

488
00:19:25,060 --> 00:19:26,300
A kind of moan.

489
00:19:26,500 --> 00:19:27,200
A cry.

490
00:19:27,340 --> 00:19:28,440
Perhaps a howl.

491
00:19:28,900 --> 00:19:32,560
I went to investigate and found myself standing at the entryway to the Roman tunnels.

492
00:19:32,940 --> 00:19:34,700
The sound came from inside.

493
00:19:34,700 --> 00:19:35,680
Oh no!

494
00:19:36,180 --> 00:19:38,380
I don't want to be hearing any sounds like that today.

495
00:19:38,960 --> 00:19:40,920
I don't want to go inside the Roman tunnels.

496
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:45,260
I dared not shine a light inside for fear of what I might see.

497
00:19:45,760 --> 00:19:49,600
And then, a scrambling thudding came racing towards me from the darkness.

498
00:19:49,960 --> 00:19:52,280
A shape loomed up out of the shadows.

499
00:19:52,700 --> 00:19:55,100
I reached for my sidearm, ready to fire.

500
00:19:55,600 --> 00:19:56,700
It was Toussaint.

501
00:19:57,660 --> 00:19:58,420
Oh shit.

502
00:19:59,220 --> 00:20:00,600
He'd been awakened as well.

503
00:20:00,940 --> 00:20:03,080
But unlike me, he dared to enter the tunnels.

504
00:20:03,540 --> 00:20:05,100
He says he saw something there.

505
00:20:05,880 --> 00:20:11,200
As we stood at that moan, listening, the howling, howling, howling grew distant.

506
00:20:12,100 --> 00:20:13,660
We're seated to where I dare not guess.

507
00:20:14,480 --> 00:20:15,760
Perhaps our minds are gone.

508
00:20:16,300 --> 00:20:18,020
Or perhaps there is something down there.

509
00:20:18,760 --> 00:20:20,120
Toussaint will not tell me what he saw.

510
00:20:20,940 --> 00:20:22,200
Please write me again soon.

511
00:20:22,360 --> 00:20:23,240
Love to you, Johannes.

512
00:20:23,940 --> 00:20:36,740
I wonder if only the people who have been exposed to the tunnel, and maybe even this liquid, are the ones able to hear these moans from the tunnel, or these voices, this howling.

513
00:20:37,420 --> 00:20:41,180
Because it seems to me like the officers don't believe any of them, right?

514
00:20:42,700 --> 00:20:44,840
In fact, they're punishing them for speaking up about it.

515
00:20:46,100 --> 00:20:48,160
And maybe the officers never went into the tunnel?

516
00:20:48,200 --> 00:20:48,740
I'm not sure.

517
00:20:49,800 --> 00:20:51,560
Maybe it is all a hallucination, you know?

518
00:20:51,560 --> 00:20:53,960
What if this monster isn't even real?

519
00:20:54,620 --> 00:20:56,260
And I'm hallucinating the monster.

520
00:20:56,660 --> 00:20:57,400
Nah, probably not.

521
00:20:57,760 --> 00:20:58,920
It's definitely real.

522
00:20:59,380 --> 00:21:01,000
He ate me, and the game was over.

523
00:21:03,100 --> 00:21:04,220
Soldat Marzot.

524
00:21:04,640 --> 00:21:06,200
The officers have fled.

525
00:21:06,380 --> 00:21:06,540
Yeah.

526
00:21:06,940 --> 00:21:08,100
Fucking assholes.

527
00:21:09,060 --> 00:21:13,160
But it's okay, because, you know, Fournier will get back to me with the code.

528
00:21:13,400 --> 00:21:13,680
Yay!

529
00:21:14,340 --> 00:21:15,180
Good job.

530
00:21:15,760 --> 00:21:16,540
Soldat Gough.

531
00:21:17,380 --> 00:21:18,800
Communications key, not interesting.

532
00:21:18,800 --> 00:21:19,520
Ozan?

533
00:21:19,900 --> 00:21:20,900
No to Farber.

534
00:21:22,940 --> 00:21:25,000
I was there when they pulled your friend Neuer from the tunnels.

535
00:21:25,560 --> 00:21:28,020
He'd been screaming for hours before he was located.

536
00:21:28,400 --> 00:21:29,520
Tied to the stretcher.

537
00:21:29,660 --> 00:21:32,680
He was still trying to scream, but all that came out was a horrible rasp.

538
00:21:33,160 --> 00:21:35,140
All of the engineers have seen things down there.

539
00:21:35,740 --> 00:21:36,520
Myself included.

540
00:21:37,060 --> 00:21:39,480
We should talk, you and I, about what is to be done.

541
00:21:39,820 --> 00:21:40,780
Let me know when.

542
00:21:41,820 --> 00:21:42,260
Ozan.

543
00:21:43,400 --> 00:21:43,840
Okay.

544
00:21:45,320 --> 00:21:45,760
Tremblay.

545
00:21:46,360 --> 00:21:47,180
Farber dies.

546
00:21:48,400 --> 00:21:51,120
Hold on, is that the person Ozan was talking to?

547
00:21:51,200 --> 00:21:52,020
Yeah, no to Farber.

548
00:21:53,600 --> 00:21:54,700
So he dies now.

549
00:21:55,440 --> 00:21:56,300
Farber is gone.

550
00:21:56,500 --> 00:21:56,940
Insanity.

551
00:21:57,080 --> 00:21:57,360
Chaos.

552
00:21:58,160 --> 00:22:01,580
We were in the mess and it burst out from the shadows right behind Borond.

553
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:03,220
But Farber was there.

554
00:22:03,480 --> 00:22:03,860
Ready.

555
00:22:04,440 --> 00:22:06,040
Practically threw himself in front of the thing.

556
00:22:06,280 --> 00:22:07,220
And he shot it!

557
00:22:07,300 --> 00:22:07,560
Hit it!

558
00:22:07,660 --> 00:22:08,000
Dead on!

559
00:22:08,360 --> 00:22:09,440
The thing retreated.

560
00:22:09,440 --> 00:22:11,080
We thought for sure it was dead.

561
00:22:11,400 --> 00:22:14,220
But then, not ten minutes later, it came back for him.

562
00:22:14,720 --> 00:22:15,680
I heard him screaming.

563
00:22:16,000 --> 00:22:17,300
Being pulled into the wall.

564
00:22:17,580 --> 00:22:18,660
Praying for salvation.

565
00:22:19,220 --> 00:22:20,880
And now I can hear it moving again.

566
00:22:21,100 --> 00:22:21,660
Getting closer.

567
00:22:22,320 --> 00:22:23,160
Have to move now.

568
00:22:23,620 --> 00:22:25,220
Or we'll all suffer his fate.

569
00:22:26,920 --> 00:22:27,860
Crazy shit.

570
00:22:29,060 --> 00:22:30,120
And then Fonier.

571
00:22:31,580 --> 00:22:34,220
Also, did I say Fonier before when I meant to say...

572
00:22:35,780 --> 00:22:36,580
What's his name?

573
00:22:37,500 --> 00:22:37,900
Joubert.

574
00:22:38,100 --> 00:22:38,740
I meant to say Joubert.

575
00:22:38,900 --> 00:22:42,280
The guy who escaped with the other officers and then threw the code back to us.

576
00:22:43,300 --> 00:22:44,860
Or relayed it back to us.

577
00:22:46,300 --> 00:22:46,700
Fonier.

578
00:22:46,880 --> 00:22:47,800
Assumptions about motive.

579
00:22:48,480 --> 00:22:49,860
So, 6th of June.

580
00:22:50,660 --> 00:22:51,060
Right.

581
00:22:51,160 --> 00:22:55,860
So, a whole month before I bring back Lambert, right?

582
00:22:56,400 --> 00:22:57,680
In fact, a little over a month.

583
00:22:58,860 --> 00:23:00,240
He's writing to Renard.

584
00:23:00,240 --> 00:23:03,540
Further to your investigation of the tunnel's sabotage.

585
00:23:03,860 --> 00:23:05,300
Your assumptions are safe.

586
00:23:05,720 --> 00:23:08,780
Start with those who spread the rumors about magic and devilry in the tunnels.

587
00:23:09,320 --> 00:23:11,640
Clearly, they've had sabotage in their minds for weeks.

588
00:23:12,280 --> 00:23:14,520
Use any means necessary to elicit confessions.

589
00:23:14,840 --> 00:23:17,020
We cannot allow this treason to go unpunished.

590
00:23:18,380 --> 00:23:19,700
It's gotta mean major then.

591
00:23:20,120 --> 00:23:20,620
Right?

592
00:23:20,880 --> 00:23:22,660
Yeah, and all the officers...

593
00:23:22,660 --> 00:23:23,360
Where's our wine?

594
00:23:23,560 --> 00:23:26,040
Of course, the officers would worry about the wine.

595
00:23:26,780 --> 00:23:29,440
This is our fourth formal request for a resupply of wine.

596
00:23:30,120 --> 00:23:30,680
Yeah, yeah, whatever.

597
00:23:31,360 --> 00:23:32,520
Morale runs on wine.

598
00:23:33,320 --> 00:23:33,480
Hmm.

599
00:23:34,720 --> 00:23:35,620
Shooting the beast.

600
00:23:35,760 --> 00:23:37,500
Yeah, this is just telling me that I can shoot it.

601
00:23:37,820 --> 00:23:39,400
And it will retreat for a while.

602
00:23:40,260 --> 00:23:42,480
Delpy is also a officer here.

603
00:23:42,640 --> 00:23:43,120
A major.

604
00:23:44,420 --> 00:23:45,240
Toussaint's fate.

605
00:23:45,940 --> 00:23:47,520
11th of June, 1916.

606
00:23:48,360 --> 00:23:54,400
In regards to the fate of the saboteur Toussaint Beaufort, LaRue has added further details to his confession.

607
00:23:55,180 --> 00:24:01,520
He now claims that upon entering the Roman tunnels that night, Toussaint confided in LaRue that he had other work to do.

608
00:24:02,220 --> 00:24:07,280
When LaRue pressed him for detail, Toussaint whispered something and pointed to his own eyes.

609
00:24:08,940 --> 00:24:09,500
Huh.

610
00:24:10,060 --> 00:24:11,260
Something about sight.

611
00:24:11,920 --> 00:24:16,020
Soon after, Toussaint split from the other saboteurs and disappeared into the darkness.

612
00:24:16,540 --> 00:24:21,460
When the others failed to locate him, they assumed he had returned to his bunk and proceeded with their plan.

613
00:24:22,020 --> 00:24:27,600
I believe it's safe to assume that Toussaint either perished in the blast or has since starved to death in the rubble.

614
00:24:30,550 --> 00:24:31,010
Oooh.

615
00:24:33,270 --> 00:24:36,130
And we have a note from Toussaint we haven't read yet.

616
00:24:37,330 --> 00:24:38,830
I have a bad feeling about this.

617
00:24:38,990 --> 00:24:39,830
Prisoner in custody.

618
00:24:41,050 --> 00:24:42,450
Is this just the German one?

619
00:24:43,070 --> 00:24:43,790
Yeah, okay.

620
00:24:44,670 --> 00:24:46,150
I wonder if he was an officer.

621
00:24:47,550 --> 00:24:48,510
Major Blanchett.

622
00:24:49,550 --> 00:24:50,890
In charge of security.

623
00:24:51,730 --> 00:24:52,810
Uh, let's see here.

624
00:24:53,570 --> 00:24:54,530
Emergency lockdown.

625
00:24:54,910 --> 00:24:55,690
Yeah, yeah, that's fine.

626
00:24:56,510 --> 00:24:56,990
Lambert.

627
00:24:57,210 --> 00:24:58,550
Lambert's journal part one.

628
00:24:59,510 --> 00:25:01,830
Oh, did I miss parts to this?

629
00:25:04,130 --> 00:25:04,890
Part one?

630
00:25:04,890 --> 00:25:05,790
I haven't found a part two.

631
00:25:05,870 --> 00:25:06,790
Maybe we'll find one down here.

632
00:25:07,430 --> 00:25:08,230
11th of July.

633
00:25:08,230 --> 00:25:11,210
So this was two days after we returned home?

634
00:25:11,670 --> 00:25:13,230
Or after he brought us home?

635
00:25:14,270 --> 00:25:14,750
Dusk.

636
00:25:16,590 --> 00:25:19,270
I sit now at the bedside of my dear friend Henri Clément.

637
00:25:19,670 --> 00:25:21,490
The doctor has left, but I remain.

638
00:25:22,150 --> 00:25:26,470
I feel I must record the extraordinary twists of fate and fortune that have led me to be here.

639
00:25:26,950 --> 00:25:28,730
Breathing, alive, strong and well.

640
00:25:28,730 --> 00:25:31,830
While Henri lies unconscious fighting for his life.

641
00:25:32,850 --> 00:25:34,610
It starts days ago on a night patrol.

642
00:25:34,950 --> 00:25:36,490
I fell into some kind of pit.

643
00:25:36,870 --> 00:25:39,570
I was injured, unable to move, unable to escape.

644
00:25:40,090 --> 00:25:42,130
By all rights, it should have been my tomb.

645
00:25:42,730 --> 00:25:43,890
I cried for help.

646
00:25:44,430 --> 00:25:45,650
Screamed to myself hoarse.

647
00:25:46,070 --> 00:25:47,470
The effort left me parched.

648
00:25:47,970 --> 00:25:49,170
Exhausted and still alone.

649
00:25:49,770 --> 00:25:53,650
As the next night fell, as I cried what might have been my last cry for help.

650
00:25:53,650 --> 00:25:56,510
I could see the stars high, high above.

651
00:25:57,190 --> 00:25:58,350
Beautiful, indifferent.

652
00:25:59,190 --> 00:26:01,570
And then Clément's face appeared at the top of the pit.

653
00:26:02,030 --> 00:26:03,450
He lowered himself to me.

654
00:26:03,870 --> 00:26:06,650
Found a trickle of spring water there and had me drink from it.

655
00:26:06,950 --> 00:26:09,990
It was cool and crisp with a strange, sweet taste.

656
00:26:10,610 --> 00:26:12,770
Never has water felt more nourishing than that.

657
00:26:13,370 --> 00:26:14,890
Administered by a dear friend's hand.

658
00:26:17,270 --> 00:26:18,290
I was saved.

659
00:26:18,470 --> 00:26:22,590
But of course, that is not the last twist fate's blade would stab into my back.

660
00:26:22,590 --> 00:26:24,570
Oh, wait a minute.

661
00:26:26,470 --> 00:26:29,750
It was cool and crisp with a strange, sweet taste.

662
00:26:32,150 --> 00:26:35,450
I must have given him the liquid of the Roman tunnels.

663
00:26:38,300 --> 00:26:40,740
Oh no, he is the monster, 100%.

664
00:26:42,740 --> 00:26:43,780
11th of July.

665
00:26:44,900 --> 00:26:46,740
Later now, I continue my tale.

666
00:26:47,120 --> 00:26:49,520
As Clément carried me across no man's land.

667
00:26:50,040 --> 00:26:51,220
Fate struck again.

668
00:26:51,440 --> 00:26:53,160
A German outpost spotted us.

669
00:26:53,360 --> 00:26:55,460
Gunfire, explosions, desperation.

670
00:26:56,320 --> 00:27:00,520
And as the air cleared, I pulled myself to my feet and saw that Henri was wounded.

671
00:27:01,120 --> 00:27:02,560
Blood pouring from his head.

672
00:27:02,780 --> 00:27:04,020
His eyes glassy.

673
00:27:04,160 --> 00:27:05,000
He was fading.

674
00:27:05,980 --> 00:27:08,340
I do not know where I found the strength to carry him.

675
00:27:08,860 --> 00:27:10,040
But carry him I did.

676
00:27:10,200 --> 00:27:11,560
All the way back to our bunker.

677
00:27:11,680 --> 00:27:13,860
Yeah, you did because you got the strength from the liquid.

678
00:27:15,060 --> 00:27:17,460
You drank that shit and now you became...

679
00:27:17,460 --> 00:27:18,240
fucking strong.

680
00:27:19,580 --> 00:27:20,560
12th of July.

681
00:27:21,300 --> 00:27:21,780
Morning.

682
00:27:22,620 --> 00:27:25,780
Woke this morning and realized that the toy I purchased from my son is gone.

683
00:27:26,140 --> 00:27:28,620
I promised him I'd bring him something home from the front.

684
00:27:28,920 --> 00:27:31,300
So I bought him a stuffed rabbit from a local shop.

685
00:27:31,580 --> 00:27:33,500
A rabbit because he thinks he's so fast.

686
00:27:34,120 --> 00:27:36,580
It must have fallen from my pack when I fell into the crater.

687
00:27:37,120 --> 00:27:39,620
The thought of that stuffed rabbit lying in that crater.

688
00:27:39,980 --> 00:27:41,740
Rain and weather matting its fur.

689
00:27:42,260 --> 00:27:43,320
Unloved, forgotten.

690
00:27:43,740 --> 00:27:45,240
Totally alone, lost forever.

691
00:27:45,240 --> 00:27:47,780
It fills me with a profound hopelessness.

692
00:27:48,740 --> 00:27:49,800
And then afternoon.

693
00:27:51,140 --> 00:27:51,820
Spoke to the doctor.

694
00:27:52,380 --> 00:27:55,900
He told me Henri woke in the night and had no recollection of the events in the crater.

695
00:27:56,480 --> 00:27:58,960
Indeed, he seemed even confused as to where he was.

696
00:27:59,780 --> 00:28:02,720
Aside from this disturbing news, I'm feeling rather good.

697
00:28:03,320 --> 00:28:04,200
Stronger and stronger.

698
00:28:04,520 --> 00:28:07,880
As if the whole ordeal has filled both my body and soul with new purpose.

699
00:28:09,060 --> 00:28:09,960
Yeah, dude.

700
00:28:10,140 --> 00:28:12,020
It's filled your whole body with evil.

701
00:28:13,120 --> 00:28:13,980
Evil strength.

702
00:28:16,060 --> 00:28:16,500
Renard.

703
00:28:18,620 --> 00:28:19,480
Neuer's translations.

704
00:28:19,800 --> 00:28:21,640
Every time I read Neuer, I think of paranoia.

705
00:28:22,180 --> 00:28:23,340
Which is fitting, I guess.

706
00:28:23,980 --> 00:28:25,480
And this is to Fournier and Blanchett.

707
00:28:26,160 --> 00:28:27,880
Okay, so a sergeant writing to a major.

708
00:28:28,900 --> 00:28:30,900
LaRue reports that Neuer is the source of the problem.

709
00:28:31,300 --> 00:28:36,860
He's going around telling the men that those damn texts contain accounts of pagan rituals performed in those tunnels.

710
00:28:37,640 --> 00:28:38,900
Ghastly and wild stories.

711
00:28:38,900 --> 00:28:43,840
Now superstition and rumors are passed around to men like an open flask or venereal disease.

712
00:28:44,520 --> 00:28:46,620
Some even say they have seen the things.

713
00:28:47,160 --> 00:28:47,660
Ghosts.

714
00:28:47,760 --> 00:28:48,180
Demons.

715
00:28:48,460 --> 00:28:48,960
Fairies.

716
00:28:50,120 --> 00:28:53,090
Instead of the Angel of Mons, I'm afraid we have the devils of Posieres.

717
00:28:53,900 --> 00:28:55,580
I've called Neuer for reprimanding.

718
00:28:55,580 --> 00:28:57,880
I'll make sure it is appropriately severe.

719
00:28:58,540 --> 00:29:00,920
Meanwhile, the engineers will continue to dig.

720
00:29:01,680 --> 00:29:02,140
Hmm.

721
00:29:03,740 --> 00:29:04,920
List of the guilty.

722
00:29:05,660 --> 00:29:06,480
9th of June.

723
00:29:07,260 --> 00:29:09,160
To Fournier from Renard.

724
00:29:10,320 --> 00:29:12,580
Sabotage has left the tunnel project in ruins.

725
00:29:12,900 --> 00:29:18,160
At approximately 23 hours 30 on 2nd of June, an explosion ripped through the tunnel system.

726
00:29:18,480 --> 00:29:21,640
It was quickly determined that explosives were missing from the arsenal.

727
00:29:21,900 --> 00:29:23,560
And the explosion was no accident.

728
00:29:24,360 --> 00:29:28,420
After a swift investigation, the following soldiers have confessed to sabotage.

729
00:29:29,000 --> 00:29:30,040
Gaspar LaRue.

730
00:29:30,700 --> 00:29:32,380
First Class Johannes Nicolet.

731
00:29:32,880 --> 00:29:33,340
Beaufoy.

732
00:29:33,600 --> 00:29:34,260
Toussaint, yeah.

733
00:29:35,240 --> 00:29:36,800
And Jean Renoir.

734
00:29:37,140 --> 00:29:38,540
And Ossain Sebel.

735
00:29:40,240 --> 00:29:40,980
Got it.

736
00:29:42,140 --> 00:29:44,840
Four of the guilty now rot in the cells awaiting tribunal.

737
00:29:45,100 --> 00:29:47,660
The fifth, Toussaint, remains unaccounted for.

738
00:29:47,900 --> 00:29:49,640
He may have been killed in the blast.

739
00:29:50,260 --> 00:29:53,480
I believe there are others involved, but as of yet no one will say anything.

740
00:29:54,060 --> 00:29:56,660
Worse than double agents, these men are cowards.

741
00:29:56,660 --> 00:29:59,600
They scream about ghosts and demons in other worlds.

742
00:29:59,860 --> 00:30:03,740
They claim they committed this act of treason to save their fellow soldiers from hell.

743
00:30:04,140 --> 00:30:05,060
Utter nonsense.

744
00:30:05,720 --> 00:30:09,080
We are still working to clear the tunnel site, and assess the damage.

745
00:30:09,380 --> 00:30:12,620
But I fear that any hope of using them for our purposes is now lost.

746
00:30:13,420 --> 00:30:17,460
In addition, the explosion has caused other structural damage to the bunker itself.

747
00:30:17,960 --> 00:30:20,160
Flooding is now occurring in various areas.

748
00:30:21,420 --> 00:30:23,120
That's why it was flooded.

749
00:30:25,100 --> 00:30:25,600
Okay.

750
00:30:27,600 --> 00:30:28,640
Update on prisoner.

751
00:30:29,000 --> 00:30:29,980
Oh, the German one.

752
00:30:30,940 --> 00:30:33,300
He continues to insist that he's not a common soldier.

753
00:30:33,620 --> 00:30:35,040
Or that he is a common soldier.

754
00:30:35,880 --> 00:30:37,640
His rank was torn from his body.

755
00:30:39,260 --> 00:30:40,240
Uh, yeah, whatever.

756
00:30:40,720 --> 00:30:41,360
That's fine.

757
00:30:42,060 --> 00:30:42,780
And why?

758
00:30:43,440 --> 00:30:44,800
After digging too deep.

759
00:30:45,020 --> 00:30:45,680
The 2nd of April.

760
00:30:45,860 --> 00:30:46,820
So this is way back.

761
00:30:47,400 --> 00:30:47,980
My friend!

762
00:30:49,180 --> 00:30:51,600
Received your message about the order to dig the bunker deeper.

763
00:30:52,140 --> 00:30:54,820
I appreciate your enthusiasm, your patriotism.

764
00:30:54,920 --> 00:30:56,020
I only wish I could share it.

765
00:30:56,460 --> 00:30:59,920
I fear command will only prove themselves fools and your men will pay the cost.

766
00:31:00,300 --> 00:31:04,100
They want a grand subterranean hub of courage, steel and intelligence.

767
00:31:05,080 --> 00:31:07,220
Okay, so this is just the order to start digging.

768
00:31:08,660 --> 00:31:09,320
Got it.

769
00:31:10,260 --> 00:31:10,560
Farber.

770
00:31:11,680 --> 00:31:12,660
Gathering of the willing.

771
00:31:13,720 --> 00:31:19,920
After what happened with Neuer, after how Renard and Fournier treated him and LaRue, there's only one way forward for us.

772
00:31:20,500 --> 00:31:22,100
I've gathered the men I can trust.

773
00:31:22,600 --> 00:31:23,900
Propose to them what we will do.

774
00:31:24,180 --> 00:31:26,060
To a man, all of them were willing.

775
00:31:26,260 --> 00:31:27,280
It was such a relief.

776
00:31:28,040 --> 00:31:30,500
T seemed eager to go, the poor man.

777
00:31:30,800 --> 00:31:33,900
I hear him at night, muttering in rhymes, trying to comfort himself.

778
00:31:34,200 --> 00:31:37,540
For his sake, for all our sakes, this nightmare must stop.

779
00:31:38,060 --> 00:31:39,820
Late now on the 14th of June.

780
00:31:40,120 --> 00:31:41,500
The nightmares have stopped.

781
00:31:41,800 --> 00:31:43,560
We no longer hear those sounds.

782
00:31:43,920 --> 00:31:45,980
But now I'm plagued by worse nightmares.

783
00:31:46,320 --> 00:31:48,420
My fellow saboteurs were all caught.

784
00:31:49,000 --> 00:31:50,780
Delpy and Renard tortured them even now.

785
00:31:51,320 --> 00:31:52,200
Oh man.

786
00:31:52,760 --> 00:31:56,180
Pretty much confirmation that the tunnels were responsible for all this.

787
00:31:56,180 --> 00:31:57,780
I mean, that was obvious, right?

788
00:31:58,820 --> 00:32:00,540
And yet none of them have turned me in.

789
00:32:00,840 --> 00:32:02,620
I alone have escaped punishment.

790
00:32:02,940 --> 00:32:05,180
The honor among these men, my brothers.

791
00:32:05,660 --> 00:32:06,880
I'm not worthy of it.

792
00:32:07,040 --> 00:32:07,960
It haunts me.

793
00:32:08,360 --> 00:32:09,380
The guilt of it.

794
00:32:09,760 --> 00:32:11,520
